The client entrypoint is in the wrong place. `src/client` is mapped to `ReplicatedStorage.Client`, and LocalScripts under ReplicatedStorage never run. Roblox only runs a LocalScript when it sits under `StarterPlayer.StarterPlayerScripts`, `StarterGui`, `StarterCharacterScripts`, or a similar container. The `print("client")` in `src/client/init.client.luau` would never fire.

The server side is fine. `src/server` maps to `ServerScriptService.Server`, and Server scripts run from there.

The fix is to give the client entrypoint its own source folder and map that folder to `StarterPlayerScripts`, and keep `src/client` for modules that the client shares. Shared client modules stay in `ReplicatedStorage.Client`, so the entry can `require` them. I'd change `default.project.json` like this:

```json
{
  "name": "arena",
  "tree": {
    "$className": "DataModel",
    "ReplicatedStorage": {
      "Shared": { "$path": "src/shared" },
      "Client": { "$path": "src/client" },
      "Packages": { "$path": "Packages" }
    },
    "ServerScriptService": { "Server": { "$path": "src/server" } },
    "StarterPlayer": {
      "StarterPlayerScripts": {
        "Client": { "$path": "src/client-entry" }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Then move `src/client/init.client.luau` to `src/client-entry/init.client.luau`. The folder name is my suggestion; any name works as long as the `$path` matches.

I haven't made these changes. Should I move the file and update the project file? I'd also add a `require` of `ReplicatedStorage.Client` from the entry so the wiring is visible, though that's optional.
